  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "If $U={2,4,6,8,\u2026,20}$ is the universal set and $B={4,8,12,16,20},$ then the complement of $B$ is",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $2,$ $6,$ $10,$ $14,$ and $18.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{B}={2,6,10,14,18}.\n$$",
